IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part III, Premiums: sections 67 to 70.1.
-- The employee's premium (s 67), the employer's premium (s 68), the reduction for wage-loss plans and provincial plans
-- (s 69) and the year to which late-paid earnings belong (s 70).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as inputs (listed in NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges"):
--   * insurable earnings (s 2(1): "determined in accordance with Part IV", the Insurable Earnings and Collection of
--     Premiums Regulations, which are not among the inputs): a NUMBER of dollars;
--   * the premium rate "set under section 66 or 66.32": a NUMBER fraction (1.63% is 0.0163), whatever year it is for;
--   * the reduction of premiums under regulations made under s 69 (regs 62 to 76.45 of the Employment Insurance
--     Regulations, piece er4): a NUMBER of dollars.

§ `Section 67 - the employee's premium`

-- "A person employed in insurable employment shall pay ... a premium": the duty arises only for such a person.
-- The caller may feed `s 5 insurable employment` (the keel) into the input.
-- src:1195 | 67 Subject to section 70, a person employed in insurable employment shall pay, by deduction as provided in subsection 82(1), a premium equal to their insurable earnings multiplied by the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 67 (src:1195)
GIVEN `is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 67 a person must pay the employee's premium` IF
    `is employed in insurable employment`

-- The amount is "their insurable earnings multiplied by the premium rate". Section 67 itself states no cap: the
-- maximum yearly insurable earnings bites through s 82(2) (the employer stops deducting) and s 95 (the excess is an
-- overpayment to be refunded).
-- src:1195 | 67 Subject to section 70, a person employed in insurable employment shall pay, by deduction as provided in subsection 82(1), a premium equal to their insurable earnings multiplied by the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 67 (src:1195)
GIVEN `insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 67 the employee's premium` IS
    `insurable earnings` TIMES `the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32`

§ `Section 68 - the employer's premium`

-- src:1197 | 68 Subject to sections 69 and 70, an employer shall pay a premium equal to 1.4 times the employees’ premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 68 (src:1197)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 68 the multiple of the employees' premiums that makes the employer's premium` MEANS 1.4

-- src:1197 | 68 Subject to sections 69 and 70, an employer shall pay a premium equal to 1.4 times the employees’ premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 68 (src:1197)
GIVEN `the employees' premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 68 the employer's premium` IS
    `s 68 the multiple of the employees' premiums that makes the employer's premium` TIMES `the employees' premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1)`

-- "Subject to sections 69 and 70": what is left once the reduction under the s 69 regulations is taken off.
-- The reduction itself is worked out by the Regulations (piece er4); here it is a dollar input.
-- src:1197 | 68 Subject to sections 69 and 70, an employer shall pay a premium equal to 1.4 times the employees’ premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 68, s 69 (src:1197)
GIVEN `the employees' premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction of the employer's premium under the regulations made under section 69` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 69 the employer's premium after the reduction` IS
    `s 68 the employer's premium` `the employees' premiums that the employer is required to deduct under subsection 82(1)`
        MINUS `the reduction of the employer's premium under the regulations made under section 69`

§ `Section 69 - premium reduction for wage-loss plans and provincial plans`

-- The reasons listed in s 69(1)(a) and (2). The last three are read through s 69(6) to (8), not by their bare words.
DECLARE `ei3 Reason for allowances, money or other benefits` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 illness`
    `ei3 injury`
    `ei3 quarantine`
    `ei3 pregnancy`
    `ei3 child care`
    `ei3 compassionate care`
    `ei3 a child's critical illness`
    `ei3 an adult's critical illness`

-- src:1218 | (6) The reference to the payment of allowances, money or other benefits because of compassionate care in subsections (1) and (2) means the payment of allowances, money or other benefits for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(6) (src:1218)
GIVEN `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(6) the payment is because of compassionate care` IF
    `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.1`

-- src:1220 | (7) The reference to the payment of allowances, money or other benefits because of a child’s critical illness in subsections (1) and (2) means the payment of allowances, money or other benefits for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.2.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(7) (src:1220)
GIVEN `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(7) the payment is because of a child's critical illness` IF
    `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.2`

-- src:1222 | (8) The reference to the payment of allowances, money or other benefits because of an adult’s critical illness in subsections (1) and (2) means the payment of allowances, money or other benefits for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.3.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(8) (src:1222)
GIVEN `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(8) the payment is because of an adult's critical illness` IF
    `the payment is for the same or substantially the same reasons for which benefits are payable under section 23.3`

-- Whether the payment is "because of" one of the listed reasons: the first five on their own words, the last three
-- through the reading rules in (6) to (8). Section 23.1, 23.2 and 23.3 belong to piece ei1; their outcome is an input.
-- src:1200 | (a) the payment of any allowances, money or other benefits because of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy, child care, compassionate care, a child’s critical illness or an adult’s critical illness under a plan that covers insured persons employed by the employer, other than one established under a provincial law, would have the effect of reducing the special benefits payable to the insured persons; and
-- src:1203 | (2) The Commission shall, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make regulations to provide a system for reducing the employer’s and employee’s premiums, the premiums under Part VII.1 or all those premiums, when the payment of any allowances, money or other benefits because of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy, child care, compassionate care, a child’s critical illness or an adult’s critical illness under a provincial law to insured persons, or to self-employed persons, as the case may be, would have the effect of reducing or eliminating the special benefits payable to those insured persons or the benefits payable to those self-employed persons.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(1)(a), s 69(2) (src:1200) (src:1203)
GIVEN reason IS A `ei3 Reason for allowances, money or other benefits`
      `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(1)(a) and (2) the payment is because of a listed reason` IS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `ei3 illness` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 quarantine` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 pregnancy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 child care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 compassionate care` THEN `s 69(6) the payment is because of compassionate care` `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.1`
    WHEN `ei3 a child's critical illness` THEN `s 69(7) the payment is because of a child's critical illness` `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.2`
    WHEN `ei3 an adult's critical illness` THEN `s 69(8) the payment is because of an adult's critical illness` `for the same or substantially the same reasons as benefits under section 23.3`

-- Paragraph (b): the insured persons must benefit by "at least equal to 5/12 of the reduction".
-- src:1201 | (b) the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer’s premium in an amount at least equal to 5/12 of the reduction.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(1)(b) (src:1201)
GIVEN `the amount by which the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction of the employer's premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` IF
    `the amount by which the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer's premium`
        AT LEAST ((5 DIVIDED BY 12) TIMES `the reduction of the employer's premium`)

-- src:1199 | 69 (1) The Commission shall, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make regulations to provide a system for reducing the employer’s premium when
-- src:1200 | (a) the payment of any allowances, money or other benefits because of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy, child care, compassionate care, a child’s critical illness or an adult’s critical illness under a plan that covers insured persons employed by the employer, other than one established under a provincial law, would have the effect of reducing the special benefits payable to the insured persons; and
-- src:1201 | (b) the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer’s premium in an amount at least equal to 5/12 of the reduction.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(1) (src:1199-1201)
GIVEN `the payment is because of a listed reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan covers insured persons employed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan is established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment would have the effect of reducing the special benefits payable to the insured persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount by which the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction of the employer's premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(1) a system for reducing the employer's premium is to be provided` IF
        `the payment is because of a listed reason`
    AND `the plan covers insured persons employed by the employer`
    AND (NOT `the plan is established under a provincial law`)
    AND `the payment would have the effect of reducing the special benefits payable to the insured persons`
    AND `s 69(1)(b) the insured persons will benefit by at least 5/12 of the reduction` `the amount by which the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer's premium` `the reduction of the employer's premium`

-- Subsection (2): which premiums the system reduces depends on to whom the provincial plan pays. "As the case may be":
-- insured persons only: the employer's and employee's premiums; self-employed persons only: the Part VII.1 premiums;
-- both: all those premiums. If nobody's benefits are reduced the subsection does not call for a reduction (NOTHING).
DECLARE `ei3 Premiums to be reduced under subsection 69(2)` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 the employer's and the employee's premiums`
    `ei3 the premiums under Part VII.1`
    `ei3 all those premiums`

-- src:1203 | (2) The Commission shall, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make regulations to provide a system for reducing the employer’s and employee’s premiums, the premiums under Part VII.1 or all those premiums, when the payment of any allowances, money or other benefits because of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy, child care, compassionate care, a child’s critical illness or an adult’s critical illness under a provincial law to insured persons, or to self-employed persons, as the case may be, would have the effect of reducing or eliminating the special benefits payable to those insured persons or the benefits payable to those self-employed persons.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(2) (src:1203)
GIVEN `the payment is made under a provincial law because of a listed reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is paid to insured persons and would reduce or eliminate their special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is paid to self-employed persons and would reduce or eliminate their benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei3 Premiums to be reduced under subsection 69(2)`
DECIDE `s 69(2) the premiums a system must reduce` IS
    IF (NOT `the payment is made under a provincial law because of a listed reason`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is paid to insured persons and would reduce or eliminate their special benefits` AND `it is paid to self-employed persons and would reduce or eliminate their benefits`
         THEN JUST `ei3 all those premiums`
         ELSE IF `it is paid to insured persons and would reduce or eliminate their special benefits`
              THEN JUST `ei3 the employer's and the employee's premiums`
              ELSE IF `it is paid to self-employed persons and would reduce or eliminate their benefits`
                   THEN JUST `ei3 the premiums under Part VII.1`
                   ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (4): "within 36 months after the time prescribed for making it" (add months, which clamps) and a
-- late application only (made after the prescribed time); good cause "throughout the period" is one BOOLEAN, as is
-- "subject to prescribed conditions".
-- src:1214 | (4) If an application for an employer’s premium reduction is made within 36 months after the time prescribed for making it, the Commission may, subject to prescribed conditions, regard the application as having been made at the prescribed time if the applicant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning at the prescribed time and ending on the day when the application was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(4) (src:1214)
GIVEN `the time prescribed for making the application` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the applicant shows there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning at the prescribed time and ending on the day the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(4) the Commission may regard the application as made at the prescribed time` IF
        `the day on which the application was made` GREATER THAN `the time prescribed for making the application`
    AND `the day on which the application was made` AT MOST (`add months` `the time prescribed for making the application` 36)
    AND `the applicant shows there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning at the prescribed time and ending on the day the application was made`
    AND `the prescribed conditions are met`

-- src:1216 | (5) The Commission may reconsider any decision relating to an employer’s premium reduction within 36 months after the date of the decision and any new decision that it makes shall apply in place of the reconsidered decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(5) (src:1216)
GIVEN `the date of the decision relating to the employer's premium reduction` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission reconsiders it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(5) the Commission may reconsider the decision` IF
    `the day on which the Commission reconsiders it` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the decision relating to the employer's premium reduction` 36)

-- "Any new decision that it makes shall apply in place of the reconsidered decision": once a new decision is made on a
-- reconsideration within the 36 months, it is the decision that applies.
-- src:1216 | (5) The Commission may reconsider any decision relating to an employer’s premium reduction within 36 months after the date of the decision and any new decision that it makes shall apply in place of the reconsidered decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 69(5) (src:1216)
GIVEN `the date of the decision relating to the employer's premium reduction` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission made a new decision on reconsideration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(5) the new decision applies in place of the reconsidered decision` IF
    `s 69(5) the Commission may reconsider the decision` `the date of the decision relating to the employer's premium reduction` `the day on which the Commission made a new decision on reconsideration`

§ `Section 70 - overlapping pay periods`

-- Earnings "paid after the end of the year in which their insurable employment occurred": the employment is deemed
-- to have occurred in the year they are paid. Paid in the same year, the two years are the same. Paid in an EARLIER
-- year than the employment, the section says nothing, so the answer is NOTHING (not covered).
-- src:1224 | 70 If insurable earnings are paid to a person after the end of the year in which their insurable employment occurred, the insurable employment is, for the purposes of determining insurable earnings and premiums payable, deemed to have occurred in the year in which the insurable earnings are paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 70 (src:1224)
GIVEN `the year in which the insurable employment occurred` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the insurable earnings are paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 70 the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` IS
    IF DATE_YEAR `the day on which the insurable earnings are paid` AT LEAST `the year in which the insurable employment occurred`
    THEN JUST (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the insurable earnings are paid`)
    ELSE NOTHING
